What changed and why (UE 5.8.4 source, read, not run):
1. Blank EngineAssociation: new projectEngineRoot walks up from the directory above the .uproject's directory to the drive root and takes the nearest engine root, as GetEngineIdentifierForProject does (DesktopPlatformBase.cpp 486-498). New isEngineRoot is the engine's test: Engine/Binaries and Engine/Build both directories (IsValidRootDirectory, 401-421). chooseEngine gets that root as a new tree argument and takes it before the highest-version step. The fallback to the highest installed engine stays for a project outside any engine tree; the doc comment says it is unreagent's, the engine has none.
2. A non-string value (number, bool, array, object, null) counts as blank. parseEngineAssociation reads the field as raw JSON and now also returns ok: false when the file holds no JSON object (invalid JSON, top-level null or array, empty file). With ok false, autodetectEngine does not walk up, because the engine returns before its search when LoadProjectFile fails.
3. A value containing / or \ is the new kind assocPath. associationPath resolves it as the engine does: \ counts as a separator; a value starting with /, with a double backslash, or with a drive letter and colon is taken as written; anything else is relative to the .uproject's directory (Paths.cpp 123-148, FPaths::IsRelative 1265-1280; a single leading backslash is relative there). A path that is no engine root names no engine. The engine does not walk up in that case either.
4. Encodings: new decodeUEText follows FFileHelper::BufferToString (FileHelper.cpp 145-185). UTF-16 LE or BE is decoded only behind its BOM and only for an even length. Everything else is read as UTF-8 with an optional UTF-8 BOM. A UTF-16 file without a BOM or with an odd length is read as UTF-8, so it is not JSON there either. The engine reads the association with TJsonReader (LoadProjectFile, 1661-1678), which refuses a trailing comma in an object, as encoding/json does. That differs from the RapidJSON reader that FProjectDescriptor and the plugin loader use.
5. The WARN no longer says "the editor may offer to convert the project". It now says the editor opens the project with the chosen engine, not the one the project names, and it claims nothing about prompts. In the 5.8.4 source and plugins, the association is resolved only by GetEngineIdentifierForProject, and the editor calls that only from SProjectBrowser::OpenProject and SHomeScreen. UnrealBuildTool's ProjectDescriptor.cs only reads and writes the field back. A Launcher install does not ship the version selector's source. Same correction in the chooseEngine doc comment and the k88 test comment (cmd/launcher/main_test.go 365-367).
6. The config.go package comment is now precise: a version is looked up in LauncherInstalled.dat, then the HKLM registry, then the default paths; a source-build id is looked up only among the HKCU registered builds; a path is relative to the .uproject's directory; a blank association names the tree the project lies in. The Info.Warnings comment was updated to match.

Choices (mine):
- An engine root without an editor binary counts as the project's engine, as the engine sees it, but it is not usable because unreagent has nothing to start there. A blank association then falls back to the highest version with a new WARN that names the tree ("blank, so its engine is the engine tree it lies in, <dir>, which has no editor binary ... build the editor there, or pin one with engineRoot"). A path association falls back with the "names no usable engine" WARN. The walk-up does not go past the first engine root, because the engine stops there too.
- No registry writes. On a hit the engine registers a tree it finds by walk-up or path under HKCU Builds with a new GUID (RegisterEngineInstallation); unreagent only reads.
- Whitespace around the association is still trimmed, as before. An all-blank value therefore walks up, while the engine would take it as an identifier. This is an edge case and is left alone.

